    },
    {
      "id": "claim_ff9163bc533f4bcd8ba3c0feda2e08e1",
      "statement": "The CLI exposes four execution channels that all wrap the same AgentRuntime entrypoints: run (CLI), serve (FastAPI HTTP), mcp (FastMCP stdio or http transport), and telegram (polling bot).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/agentforge/cli/main.py#L102-L309",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:265243cdba2a516857bfc8015f85cf0530e7d7c6aa095fdb29c4b6b691a1f29a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_866e3581854f487491cd69346a16042c",
      "statement": "The HTTP channel is a FastAPI app exposing POST /run (input, optional metadata; returns agent_id, output, latency_ms, provider, model, tool_calls_log) and GET /health; the Telegram channel runs an async polling bot that replies with the agent output and appends a warning if guardrail_violations are present; the MCP server (FastMCP) exposes collect_system_health, read_log_tail, scan_directory, and run_agent.",
      "evidence": [
